{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794763733,"nonce":"G06JLw2sKC6YRNwT9tJBLJFyIHs=","title":"A dropdown anchored upward opens off the top of the window: the overlay stack's layer is zero-sized when its entry arrives","message":"Reported by the owner: a menubar near the bottom edge of the window does not open its dropdowns. Reproduced in a headless session of the real cn demo (cn_demo_costs, COSTS_MENUBAR_SCROLL=130) and in blinc_recorder's menubar_hover_scroll.\n\n`position_wrapper` (overlay_stack.rs) opens a panel upward when there is under 96 px below its anchor, and did so with `.bottom(viewport.1 - y + margin)` on an absolutely placed wrapper. That is relative to the height of the parent, the `__cn_overlay_stack_layer__` div, which `build_overlay_layer` sizes to the viewport only when it is built with entries in it. In the session the layer was 0 x 0 with the dropdown inside it (ancestor chain: content, two wrappers, layer at 0,0,0,0, root), so the panel's top was 0 - 14 - 215 = -229, above the window. A panel opened downward is placed by its top and was never affected.\n\nFixed in the placement: the upward panel is in a box from the top of the viewport to just above the anchor, at its bottom, so it no longer depends on the layer's size (d-commit \"an upward dropdown...\"). After it, the cn demo's dropdown is at y 671 against a trigger at 862 to 890, inside the window.\n\nNot fixed: the layer itself. It is built zero-sized and an entry pushed afterwards does not resize it. Anything else that positions against its size would be wrong the same way. It may also be why the first open of a menu differs from later ones (the owner reports that the first browse along the menubar offsets the scroll to the top of the screen; a page scroll that did not move in the session, so this is a guess that the panel was the thing at the top).\n\nAlso seen at this commit and at 5bbfd6d6, so not new: blinc_cn::theming_precedence a_fluent_call_beats_a_stylesheet_rule and removing_a_rule_restores_the_components_default fail under --run-ignored all (the stylesheet radius, 20, wins over rounded(3)).\n\nLabels: bug, area:cn, area:layout.","files":null}]}